---
description: Branch-per-chat git workflow and commit conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

Three directives that apply before you touch anything:

- **Branch before your first edit** from the right integration branch. Fetch and pull
  `main` and `staging`; branch off `staging` when it is ahead of `main`, otherwise off
  `main` when they are in sync. If they diverge, stop and ask. Name branches
  `<type>/<slug>` (`feat|fix|docs|chore|tokens`). Read-only chats do not need a branch.
- **Never commit to `main`.**
- **Never push or open a pull request unless asked in that turn.** You create the branch
  and the commits; the human pushes and opens the PR.

Full conventions — commit message style, the git worktree setup for running multiple
chats in parallel, and cleanup — live in `Agents/context/git-workflow.md`. Read it before
committing or before starting a second concurrent thread.
